    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Welcome to 25920!</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The distance from the lowest submarine to the highest airplane</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >(In America units of course)</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Your goal is to destroy the enemy craft before they do the same to you.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Whoever loses all Submarines OR Boats OR Planes first loses the game.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Why? Because war is all about terrain superiority, and how</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >could you fight with no craft?</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Now this isn't like those other grid based water craft guessing games. There are abilities, boons, and several other twists thrown in to make it a unique game each time.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Play against the computer or locally with a friend. Can you beat Alexander the great if Alexander had battleships? Can you beat your snot nosed cousin after family dinner? (Probably that kid is an idiot)</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >There are submarines AND boats AND planes in ONE game. What more is there to say?</p>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Welcome to 25920!</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The distance from the lowest submarine to the highest airplane</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >(In America units of course)</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Your goal is to destroy the enemy craft before they do the same to you.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Whoever loses all Submarines OR Boats OR Planes first loses the game.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Why? Because war is all about terrain superiority, and how</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >could you fight with no craft?</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Now this isn't like those other grid based water craft guessing games. There are abilities, boons, and several other twists thrown in to make it a unique game each time.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Play against the computer or locally with a friend. Can you beat Alexander the great if Alexander had battleships? Can you beat your snot nosed cousin after family dinner? (Probably that kid is an idiot)</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >There are submarines AND boats AND planes in ONE game. What more is there to say?</p>",
    "short_description": "Three dimensional grid turn-based strategy game. Combat the computer or your friends to prove your brain is less smooth than theirs.",
